    <meta property="og:title" content="Adaptive oncogenesis of β-catenin emerges from declining liver tissue integrity - Nature Communications"/>
    <meta property="og:description" content="Despite being a common driver of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC), oncogenic &#946;-catenin is ineffective at initiating liver cancer on its own. Here the authors show that &#946;-catenin mutations as a single genetic event confer negative fitness in the healthy liver, while driving clonal expansion and tumorigenesis as liver tissue integrity declines with chronic liver disease or aging."/>
